{"schemaVersion": 1, "id": "c7ff6a0a-6792-4885-bdc7-ec8b557239ad", "title": "Show how chaos works with the Lorenz attractor: two trajectories that start almost at the same point", "revision": 10763, "status": "complete", "provider": "pi", "createdAt": "2026-11-23T13:49:00.892Z", "scenes": [{"id": "beat-1", "index": 0, "source": "const W=s=>s.trim().split(/\\s+/).map(Number);\n// DOPRI5 Lorenz samples, spaced by 1/8 model second, in tenths.\nconst blue=W(`310310010 328360014 410518110 483395477 312211325 245219260 221205250 205197274 206216294 222234276\n229227251 218206247 203196275 206218295 223235276 230227249 218204246 202195276 206219297 224237275\n230227247 218203245 201193278 206220298 225238274 231228245 218202243 200192279 206221300 226240274\n232228243 218201242 199191280 205222302 228241274 234229241 218200240 198189280 205223304 228243274\n235230239 219200237 197187280 204223306 229245274 236232237 220200234 196185280 203223309 230247275\n238234236 221200230 195182278 201222312 231249277 240237234 223202226 195178275 198220315 231252280\n242240234 226204221 195175269 195217319 230254284 245244234 230208215 197172261 191211322 228256290\n247249236 235214210 200171248 186201323 224258299 250255240 241223205 206173232 181187320 218257311\n251263247 249234202 216181212 179168305 206250328 250270260 256248204 231198192 183152272 189230345\n244277281 263264214 248224178 202157217 169182343 225278317 267280236 267255179 237199165 177132263\n181236366 254296283 280285205 275261153 243202139 172114252 174244386 264313286 296307203 303307145\n309317105 328354082 387462124 471470392 362259349 285255243 257235192 219178199 173158308 205256336\n256279259 265259197 242211172 189143240 174210359 241287299 273281220 268254167 234192159 170126278\n186252369 262302275 286291198 283274144 260229117 196125180 147182394 246322322 301322226 319332165\n344376136 406470198 445410383 357290316 308291223 297293160 291285115 275254088 224158112 133102354\n219329369 308343253 337357194 371409186 423453284 408358349 348317274 331332205 347371167 395445202\n436428347 376316325 328311237 323330175 344373143 402463197 444419373 363296320 313296227 304303163\n306310117 317331086 352401085 445527251 426313416 307251282 267247211 237205189 189152256 182217347\n239277291 264268220 253232179 211165202 168166330 216272330 264283246 270262185 245213160 187135233\n170211369 245296300 280290217 279270159 255224132 192127199 154193387 246313314 294311222 306312159\n317330116 347388103 427505217 441360414 328265296 284265212 261238166 217168182 162148327 211277343\n270295251 282280182 269248140 224170151 153124323 205289362 281313256 302309182 309316131 325345099\n372434116 461501334 391284375 300263256 271254191 241206169 185138248 176220363 246291293 276282214\n270256161 237195151 170121270 183251375 264306278 290297199 291287143 279263106 240189106 152087278\n185289398 289337273 323340200 349378165 402453214 435413357 368311315 325312229 323332169 347379141\n408470208 441403380 355293311 311296221 303301158 303306113 310318082 331361067 401488135 473431429\n341245330 273246238 244219201 204167234 180190327 222262309 255265241 251235196 216178207 176165309\n207254331 254274258 260252200`);\nconst wide=W(`311310010 330363014 415525120 479378478 307212320 243219259 221205250 204197275 207217294 223234275\n229226250 218205248 203196276 207219295 224235275 229226248 218204247 202195278 207220296 225237274\n230227246 217201246 201194279 206221298 226238273 231227244 217201244 200193280 206222300 227240273\n232228242 217200242 199191281 206223302 228241272 233228240 218199240 198189282 205224304 229243272\n235229238 218199238 197187282 205224306 230245273 236231236 219199235 196185282 203224309 231247273\n238233235 220199231 195182280 202224312 231250275 240236233 223200226 194179277 199222315 231252278\n242239233 225203221 194175272 196219319 231255282 245243233 229207215 196172263 192213322 229257288\n247249234 234213210 199170251 187203324 226258297 250255238 241222204 205172233 181188322 219258310\n252262245 248233202 215180213 178169308 208251327 251270258 256247203 230197192 183152274 190232345\n245278280 264263213 248224177 202156218 169183344 226278316 267280235 267256178 237199164 177131262\n181236367 254296284 281286205 276263153 245205136 175114243 171238389 262314289 297308205 305310147\n314325107 341377091 417500186 454383423 332258308 280259221 255231177 211164201 167165332 216274330\n266285245 271264183 248216156 190135224 166204370 243298305 281293219 283277160 264238126 209145163\n146150369 229312339 293318237 311320171 327347129 370424135 448490310`);\nconst medium=blue.slice(0,112).concat(W(`388463124 471469393 362259348 285255243 257235192 219178199 173158309 205257336\n256279259 265259197 242211172 189143240 174210359 241288299 273281220 268254167 234192158 170126277\n186252369 262302275 287292198 284275144 261231117 198127176 146177393 245322324 301323227 319332166\n345376137 406470200 444410382 357290315 309292223 299295159 294289115 282267085 244192087 149073270\n182299409 297348276 334355208 365398190 414449263 415377347 358322287 336334217 349371178 393439208\n432428337 380325325 334318242 331340182 357392161 416467243 427380370 352303294 319311213 322332157\n347382132 413479211 442393390 348286307 304289217 294287155 283269114 251209102 170092225 162249414\n275336292 318336210 341365166 387437188 438445334`));\nmedium[55]=240236234;medium[72]=200171249;medium[75]=250255239;\nconst small=blue.slice(0,148).concat(W(`224158111 133101353 218329369 307343253 337357194 371409186 423453284 408358349 348317274 331332205 347371167 395445203\n436428347 376316325 328311237 323330175 344374143 402463197 444418374 362296320 313296227 304303162\n306311117 318333086 356407088 450527267 419304410 304252277 267246208 236203188 187150259 183220348\n241278289 265268218 253232177 210164202 167166333 217274329 266284245 271263183 247214157 189135228\n168208370 244297303 281292218 282275159 261233127 203138174 148165378 236313330 294316232 310318167\n325343125 366418127 447498297 407313382 316275266 288275191 270250145 228177151 157121309 199281366\n277311261 298305186 303307133 310318096 329357076 393473129 472454409`));\nsmall[136]=147181394;\n\nconst world=(x,y,z)=>[(x+y)*.06788225,(z-25)*.096,(x-y)*.06788225];\nconst cloud=[[136,88,382],[-56,-49,247],[-15,-28,189],[70,46,282],[61,0,314],[-127,-159,287],[131,135,328],[-117,-159,259],[94,122,243],[-102,-157,211],[-140,-89,390],[18,-4,239],[-138,-90,384],[37,25,236],[139,106,373],[38,-47,321],[-130,-152,303],[103,63,334],[96,-3,374],[-34,-58,131],[-24,-30,181],[3,6,135],[31,53,217],[-27,-30,193],[5,-6,205],[33,5,258],[-139,-203,264],[-117,-108,321],[-53,-33,263],[-144,-73,408]].flatMap(([x,y,z])=>world(x/10,y/10,z/10));\n\nfunction spline(data,g){\n  return data.map((w,i)=>{\n    const x=i?(Math.floor(w/1e6)-300)/10:1+g;\n    const y=(Math.floor(w/1000)%1000-300)/10,z=w%1000/10;\n    return [x,y,z,10*(y-x)/8,(x*(28-z)-y)/8,(x*y-8*z/3)/8];\n  });\n}\nfunction point(a,k){\n  k=Math.max(0,Math.min(k,a.length-1));\n  const i=Math.min(Math.floor(k),a.length-2),u=k-i;\n  const h=u*u*(3-2*u),p=a[i],q=a[i+1],c=u*(1-u)*(1-u),d=-u*u*(1-u);\n  const f=j=>p[j]+h*(q[j]-p[j])+c*p[3+j]+d*q[3+j];\n  return world(f(0),f(1),f(2));\n}\n// Cue times (s) for the rewritten narration.\nconst T={'beat-1.u1.w37':38.684,'beat-1.u2.w1':44.32666666666667,'beat-1.u2.w4':45.54566666666666};\nconst C={go:11.424,ff:24.393,slow:29.78,gap:38.684,fork:46.962666666666664,end:62.275};\n// Continue a sampled path with the same Lorenz rule (RK4, 32 substeps per knot)\n// so both beads keep moving after the sampled data ends.\nfunction extend(S,n){\n  const out=S.slice(),f=(x,y,z)=>[10*(y-x),x*(28-z)-y,x*y-8*z/3],h=1/256;\n  let [x,y,z]=out[out.length-1];\n  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){\n    for(let j=0;j<32;j++){\n      const a=f(x,y,z),b=f(x+h/2*a[0],y+h/2*a[1],z+h/2*a[2]);\n      const c=f(x+h/2*b[0],y+h/2*b[1],z+h/2*b[2]),d=f(x+h*c[0],y+h*c[1],z+h*c[2]);\n      x+=h/6*(a[0]+2*b[0]+2*c[0]+d[0]);y+=h/6*(a[1]+2*b[1]+2*c[1]+d[1]);z+=h/6*(a[2]+2*b[2]+2*c[2]+d[2]);\n    }\n    out.push([x,y,z,10*(y-x)/8,(x*(28-z)-y)/8,(x*y-8*z/3)/8]);\n  }\n  return out;\n}\nconst B=extend(spline(blue,0),40);\n// [path, last knot where the trails still overlap, split knot, settled knot]\nconst pairs={\n  '0.1':[spline(wide,.1),102,132.4,135.9],\n  '0.001':[spline(medium,.001),145,180.5,183.8],\n  '0.00001':[spline(small,.00001),192,211.8,215.1]\n};\n\nexport default scene({\n  mode:'2d',orbit:false,background:'BLACK',end:'hold',\n  audio:'6372e683f11bf45527c0a4a69c38284df73466b90169df8fbe6b51fcded1c22b.beat-1'\n},s=>{\n  // Demo: rotation is the only interaction.\n  const key='0.001';\n  const [G0,overlap,split,last]=pairs[key];\n  const G=extend(G0,70);\n  const a=n=>T['beat-1.u1.w'+n],b=n=>T['beat-1.u2.w'+n];\n\n  // Knots are 1/8 model second; speeds are knots per second and change\n  // linearly between nodes. Calm loops, fast-forward, slow look while the\n  // trails overlap, the gap opening into the split, then both keep looping.\n  const vm=3.5,vs=1.5,vp=2.5;\n  const nodes=[[C.go,0,0]];\n  function ramp(t,v){\n    const [l,k,w]=nodes[nodes.length-1];\n    nodes.push([t,k+(t-l)*(w+v)/2,v]);\n  }\n  ramp(C.go+1,vm);\n  ramp(C.ff,vm);\n  const Ka=overlap-vs*(C.gap-C.slow),k0=nodes[nodes.length-1][1];\n  const vf=(Ka-k0-.4*vm-.6*vs)/(C.slow-C.ff-1);\n  ramp(C.ff+.8,vf);\n  ramp(C.slow-1.2,vf);\n  ramp(C.slow,vs);\n  ramp(C.gap,vs);\n  const vg=(last-overlap-vs/2-vp/4)/(C.fork-C.gap-.75);\n  ramp(C.gap+1,vg);\n  ramp(C.fork-.5,vg);\n  ramp(C.fork,vp);\n  ramp(C.end,vp);\n\n  function clock(t){\n    if(t<=nodes[0][0])return 0;\n    for(let j=1;j<nodes.length;j++){\n      const [r,,v]=nodes[j];\n      if(t<=r){\n        const [l,k,w]=nodes[j-1],dt=t-l;\n        return k+dt*(w+.5*(v-w)*dt/(r-l));\n      }\n    }\n    return nodes[nodes.length-1][1];\n  }\n\n  s.view('butterfly-view',{\n    rect:[.32,.055,.675,.89],orbit:true,orbitHitTest:'geometry',\n    camera:{yaw:.13,pitch:.12,height:7.58,distance:21}\n  },v=>{\n    v.sphere('grab-surface',{radius:3.54,fill:'WHITE',opacity:.029,stroke:'none'});\n    const rim=v.path('rotation-shell',{\n      billboard:true,\n      points:Array.from({length:97},(_,i)=>[3.54*Math.cos(i*Math.PI/48),3.54*Math.sin(i*Math.PI/48),0]),\n      stroke:'GREY_D',strokeWidth:.014,opacity:.48,fill:'none'\n    });\n    v.behavior(rim,{type:'drag',plane:'xy',bounds:{min:[0,0,0],max:[0,0,0]}});\n    v.path('butterfly-guide',{\n      points:Array.from({length:1329},(_,i)=>point(B,106+i/8)),\n      stroke:'GREY_B',strokeWidth:.012,opacity:.5,fill:'none'\n    });\n\n    function trace(data,id,color,gold){\n      // One recent revolution, not a two-wing ten-knot history. At the\n      // default reading cue even the oldest sample is past the crossing.\n      const tail=k=>Array.from({length:57},(_,i)=>point(data,k-(56-i)*.1));\n      const trail=v.path(id+'-trail',{\n        points:tail(0),stroke:color,strokeWidth:gold ? .034 : .132,fill:'none'\n      });\n      v.bind(trail,[v.time],t=>({points:tail(clock(t))}));\n      const halo=v.sphere(id+'-halo',{\n        radius:gold ? .139 : .201,fill:color,opacity:gold ? .18 : .39,stroke:'none'\n      });\n      const bead=v.sphere(id,{\n        radius:gold ? .104 : .095,fill:color,stroke:'none',\n        material:{emissive:color,emissiveIntensity:.7,roughness:.28}\n      });\n      for(const h of [halo,bead])v.bind(h,[v.time],t=>({position:point(data,clock(t))}));\n    }\n    trace(B,'blue-run','BLUE',false);\n    trace(G,'gold-run','GOLD',true);\n  });\n\n  const col=[-.342,0];\n  const label=(id,text,y,fontSize,fill='WHITE')=>\n    s.text(id,{text,position:[0,y],viewportOffset:col,fontSize,fill});\n  label('eyebrow','LORENZ  ATTRACTOR',2.52,.23,'GREY_B');\n  label('title','Which wing?',1.95,.52);\n  s.line('rule',{points:[[-1.16,1.5],[1.16,1.5]],viewportOffset:col,stroke:'GREY_D',strokeWidth:.015});\n  const now=label('position-key','Bead = position now',.95,.275);\n  const past=label('history-key','Trail = past positions',.44,.275,'GREY_A');\n  label('orbit-hint','Drag to rotate',-.91,.235,'GREY_B');\n\n  let cursor=0;\n  const until=t=>{s.wait(t-cursor);cursor=t;};\n  until(a(37));\n  s.remove(now);\n  s.remove(past);\n  label('later','Later turn',1,.34);\n  until(b(1));\n  label('return','Blue circles back',.46,.29,'BLUE');\n  until(b(4));\n  label('across','Gold crosses over',-.03,.29,'GOLD');\n  until(62.275);\n});", "assets": {}, "duration": 62.275, "audio": {"id": "6372e683f11bf45527c0a4a69c38284df73466b90169df8fbe6b51fcded1c22b.beat-1", "url": "/data/c7ff6a0a-6792-4885-bdc7-ec8b557239ad-beat-1-6372e683f11b.wav"}, "narration": "Imagine dropping two leaves into swirling air, side by side. These beads are our two leaves, blue and gold, starting so close together that they look like one. The grey butterfly shows where the air carries them: round and round one wing, sometimes jumping to the other, never repeating exactly. Both follow exactly the same rule. No randomness, no luck. Let’s fast-forward. Loop after loop, they stay together. Now, slow down. Look closely: there’s a thin gold line inside the blue trail. That’s the gold bead, still right on top of blue. But every loop stretches the gap between them a little more. Watch. Blue circles back, but gold crosses to the other wing! From here on, their futures have nothing in common. That’s chaos: the rule is perfectly exact, yet any tiny difference snowballs. It’s why weather forecasts blur after about a week: we can never measure the air perfectly.", "visualDescription": "Content needed: Open on the whole butterfly in 3D. Two bright beads mark positions at the same instant; their trails show where they’ve been. Save the contrasting wing choices for the reveal.\nNotes: Assume the viewer can follow a moving dot but may not distinguish a whole path from a position on it. Begin with the beads, not the equations.\n", "words": [{"id": "beat-1.u1.w1", "text": "Imagin